<title>UK: Compass buys stake in French group.</title>
<headline>Compass buys stake in French group.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British food services company Compass Group Plc said on Tuesday it bought 11.17 percent of Compagnie Generale de Restauration as part of a cooperation agreement with France's Compagnie Generale des Eaux.</p>
<p>Compass said it paid a total 247 million francs for the stake. It said a payment of 80 million francs would be made at completion of the deal with further payments due in October, October 1998 and December 1999.</p>
<p>Compass said Compagnie Generale de Restauration employed more than 220,000 people.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
